+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G6v6nAYQAwaPgNhu6LQzSL","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Phase 5: Retry with Backoff\n2\t\n3\tAdd automatic retry functionality so that failed tasks can be re-attempted with increasing delays.\n4\t\n5\t## Requirements\n6\t\n7\t- There should be a way to mark a processing task as completed or failed.\n8\t- When a task fails and has retries remaining, it is automatically re-added to the queue with a delay.\n9\t- The delay follows exponential backoff: `baseDelay * 2^(attempt - 1)` (e.g., 1s, 2s, 4s, ...).\n10\t- The default maximum number of retries is 3, but this should be configurable per task.\n11\t- The base backoff delay defaults to 1000ms but should be configurable per task.\n12\t- The task should track how many times it has been attempted.\n13\t- Retried tasks keep their original queue and priority.\n14\t- If all retries are exhausted, the task remains in a failed state.\n15\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"20aeb57a-18a3-4f7d-96c4-d858fa822389","uuid":"aa1791a1-4b1f-4698-ae0d-aecb15f40028","timestamp":"2026-05-31T00:39:38.890Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/phases/phase-05.md","content":"# Phase 5: Retry with Backoff\n\nAdd automatic retry functionality so that failed tasks can be re-attempted with increasing delays.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- There should be a way to mark a processing task as completed or failed.\n- When a task fails and has retries remaining, it is automatically re-added to the queue with a delay.\n- The delay follows exponential backoff: `baseDelay * 2^(attempt - 1)` (e.g., 1s, 2s, 4s, ...).\n- The default maximum number of retries is 3, but this should be configurable per task.\n- The base backoff delay defaults to 1000ms but should be configurable per task.\n- The task should track how many times it has been attempted.\n- Retried tasks keep their original queue and priority.\n- If all retries are exhausted, the task re