+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015dnD7UvVeKsYWFZZ3W6nPF","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Phase 7: Task Dependencies\n2\t\n3\tAdd the ability for tasks to declare dependencies on other tasks, so they only become available once their prerequisites are done.\n4\t\n5\t## Requirements\n6\t\n7\t- When adding a task, you can specify a list of task IDs that must complete before this task becomes available.\n8\t- A task with unresolved dependencies is blocked and will not be returned when retrieving.\n9\t- When a dependency completes, the system should check whether any blocked tasks are now unblocked.\n10\t- Circular dependencies (direct or indirect) must be detected and rejected at task-creation time.\n11\t- Depending on a non-existent task should cause an error.\n12\t- A failed dependency does NOT automatically fail its dependents -- they remain blocked.\n13\t- There should be a way to inspect a task's dependency status.\n14\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"20aeb57a-18a3-4f7d-96c4-d858fa822389","uuid":"0bc05ece-783a-4507-a9fe-766989eb0768","timestamp":"2026-05-31T00:39:39.677Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/phases/phase-07.md","content":"# Phase 7: Task Dependencies\n\nAdd the ability for tasks to declare dependencies on other tasks, so they only become available once their prerequisites are done.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- When adding a task, you can specify a list of task IDs that must complete before this task becomes available.\n- A task with unresolved dependencies is blocked and will not be returned when retrieving.\n- When a dependency completes, the system should check whether any blocked tasks are now unblocked.\n- Circular dependencies (direct or indirect) must be detected and rejected at task-creation time.\n- Depending on a non-existent task should cause an error.\n- A failed dependency does NOT automatically fail its dependents -- they remain blocked.\n- There should be a way to inspect a task's dependency status.\n","numLines":14,"startLine":1,"totalLines":14}}}
+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CiK89Ksmj9nCg4iyAdiyKh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Phase 8: Concurrency Control\n2\t\n3\tAdd per-queue limits on how many tasks can be processed at the same time.\n4\t\n5\t## Requirements\n6\t\n7\t- Each queue can have a maximum concurrency setting that limits how many tasks can be in a processing state simultaneously.\n8\t- If the concurrency limit is reached, retrieving a task returns `null` even if pending tasks are available.\n9\t- Completing or failing a task frees up a concurrency slot.\n10\t- By default, queues have no concurrency limit (unlimited).\n11\t- There should be a way to set and query the concurrency limit and current active count for a queue.\n12\t- Concurrency interacts correctly with priority ordering -- the highest-priority available task is still chosen, subject to the concurrency limit.\n13\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"20aeb57a-18a3-4f7d-96c4-d858fa822389","uuid":"b71ee517-83c1-4a30-a51b-eb0992163aec","timestamp":"2026-05-31T00:39:39.676Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/phases/phase-08.md","content":"# Phase 8: Concurrency Control\n\nAdd per-queue limits on how many tasks can be processed at the same time.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Each queue can have a maximum concurrency setting that limits how many tasks can be in a processing state simultaneously.\n- If the concurrency limit is reached, retrieving a task returns `null` even if pending tasks are available.\n- Completing or failing a task frees up a concurrency slot.\n- By default, queues have no concurrency limit (unlimited).\n- There should be a way to set and query the concurrency limit and current active count for a queue.\n- Concurrency interacts correctly with priority ordering -- the highest-priority available task is still chosen, subject to the concurrency limit.\n","numLines":13,"startLine":1,"totalLines":13}}}
