+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HxAMvLWQZwgtF9uJJZQRds","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Phase 10: Recurring Tasks\n2\t\n3\tAdd the ability to schedule tasks that recur on a regular interval using simple cron-like expressions.\n4\t\n5\t## Requirements\n6\t\n7\t- A schedule associates a cron expression with a queue and a task template (the payload to use each time).\n8\t- Support a simple subset of cron expressions:\n9\t  - `*/N * * * *` -- every N minutes\n10\t  - `0 * * * *` -- every hour on the hour\n11\t  - `0 0 * * *` -- every day at midnight\n12\t- There should be a way to create, remove, and list active schedules.\n13\t- A manual \"tick\" or \"check\" mechanism should evaluate all active schedules and enqueue tasks for any that are due. This is used for testing.\n14\t- Once enqueued, recurring tasks are regular tasks subject to all other queue rules.\n15\t- Removing a schedule stops future occurrences from being created.\n16\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"20aeb57a-18a3-4f7d-96c4-d858fa822389","uuid":"15fd6dce-4558-448a-941b-0d8382690c54","timestamp":"2026-05-31T00:39:42.573Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/phases/phase-10.md","content":"# Phase 10: Recurring Tasks\n\nAdd the ability to schedule tasks that recur on a regular interval using simple cron-like expressions.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- A schedule associates a cron expression with a queue and a task template (the payload to use each time).\n- Support a simple subset of cron expressions:\n  - `*/N * * * *` -- every N minutes\n  - `0 * * * *` -- every hour on the hour\n  - `0 0 * * *` -- every day at midnight\n- There should be a way to create, remove, and list active schedules.\n- A manual \"tick\" or \"check\" mechanism should evaluate all active schedules and enqueue tasks for any that are due. This is used for testing.\n- Once enqueued, recurring tasks are regular tasks subject to all other queue rules.\n- Removing a schedule stops future occurrences from being created.\n","numLines":16,"startLine":1,"totalLines":16}}}
